description:
Stacks on m80-tv7i: replace the host-side stat-poll for `<vsock_uds>_<port>` with an inotify watch (CREATE on the chroot dir) so the kernel wakes us the instant the companion file appears. Zero CPU between events; sub-millisecond wakeup vs the 10 ms poll bound from m80-tv7i.

## Cost comparison

| approach | wakeup latency | CPU between events |
|---|---|---|
| stat poll (m80-tv7i) | ~10 ms (poll interval) | ~1 µs/probe |
| inotify | <1 ms (kernel notify) | 0 |

## Design (one function, two phases, fallback inline)

```rust
let chroot = vsock_uds.parent().expect("chroot dir");
let companion_name = format!("{}_{port}", vsock_uds.file_name()?);
let inotify = Inotify::init()?;                       // EMFILE / unsupported -> fall back to stat poll
let _watch = inotify.add_watch(chroot, WatchMask::CREATE)?;
// TOCTOU: file may have appeared between bind() (already done) and add_watch.
if chroot.join(&companion_name).exists() { /* go */ }
loop {
    let mut buf = [0u8; 1024];
    let events = inotify.read_events_blocking_with_timeout(&mut buf, deadline_remaining)?;
    if events.iter().any(|e| e.name.as_deref() == Some(OsStr::new(&companion_name))) { break; }
}
// then one-shot Channel::open_uds_only.
```

## TOCTOU note

Window: between guestd's `VsockListener::bind` (which makes Firecracker create the companion) and our `add_watch` arming, the file may already exist. We MUST stat once after add_watch and break early on hit, otherwise we wait forever on an event that already fired.

## Linux-only

This crate path is Linux-only. m80-preflight gates the OS, so we don't need cross-platform abstractions; document the Linux requirement in the crate README.

## Acceptance

- inotify dep added to m80-vsock with rationale (raw `inotify` crate vs `notify`).
- Phase: `add_watch` then stat-once for TOCTOU; then blocking read with deadline_remaining.
- Fallback inline: if `Inotify::init` or `add_watch` fails (EMFILE, fs without inotify), fall back to m80-tv7i's stat-poll loop in the same function. No abstraction layer.
- Bench shows ready latency drop vs m80-tv7i baseline (host-side wakeup p50/p95). Honest framing: marginal vs m80-tv7i alone (~10 ms -> <1 ms); meaningful when stacked with m80-6a0q minimal-init.
- Unit test: simulate the file appearing partway through (after add_watch but before first read) — must succeed via TOCTOU stat without a spurious timeout.

## Relationship

Stacks on m80-tv7i (now an explicit blocks dep). m80-tv7i alone gets us SmolVM-class. This bead gets us strictly better, with a clean fallback to m80-tv7i if inotify is unavailable.
